{{!-- Six stat tiles across. Params: pairs (CharacterSnapshot.statPairs) — the six in the order the
      debilities' brackets span them, so a tile knows whether its pair's debility is marked.

      The tile shows the ABBREVIATION, and it shows it once. Measured, six across, in real Chrome:
      "Constitution" is 96px in a 96px tile — flush, with nothing left for a letter-spacing change or
      a face that loads a shade wider — and German's "Geschicklichkeit" overruns by 22px. Both the
      tile and the label are in rem, so that ratio holds at every Font Size step rather than only at
      the default. The tile carried BOTH the name and the abbreviation once; six redundant lines.

      The abbreviation is the roll button, as a steading rating's name is: one control, so a stat
      that rolls cannot come to look like one that doesn't, and nothing has to be kept in step. It
      has to BE a <button> — core binds only `click` for these, so a <span> was keyboard-dead and
      nothing about a span said so.

      The full name is not lost: it names the button for assistive tech, and the hover still carries
      what the stat covers and when to roll it.

      A marked debility dims the two tiles it hinders — the consequence, once there is one; the bracket
      under them is what says the mapping beforehand. The folded line does the same. --}}
<div class="stonetop-stats-row">
	{{#each pairs}}
	{{#each stats}}
	<div class="stonetop-stat{{#if ../debility.active}} is-hindered{{/if}}" data-stat="{{key}}">
		<button type="button" class="stonetop-stat-roll rollable" data-roll="{{key}}"
		        aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.a11y.rollStatNamed' stat=name}}"
		        data-tooltip="{{description}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP">{{abbr}}</button>
		<input class="stonetop-stat-input" type="number"
		       aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.a11y.statValue' stat=name}}"
		       name="system.stats.{{key}}.value"
		       value="{{value}}" min="-3" max="3"
		       {{#unless @root.editable}}disabled{{/unless}}>
	</div>
	{{/each}}
	{{/each}}
</div>
